00:03:17.557 --> 00:03:19.960
"How a Career in Consulting Looks Like"

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:21.780
and I will link it somewhere above here.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:23.900
So, check this out if
this is all new to you

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:25.750
and you really wanna
understand a bit better

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:28.710
how the whole career path
in consulting looks like.

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:30.690
So, the first role I wanna talk about

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:32.310
is the business analyst role.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:34.690
And how exactly these roles are called,

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:36.550
changes a bit firm by firm,

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:38.380
they all have their own terminology

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:39.640
though in the end is all the same, right?

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:40.990
And the business analyst role

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:43.330
is the role that you will
have fresh out of university.

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:46.320
If you need for university with
a bachelor or master degree

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:48.350
you just start out in consulting,

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:49.680
this is the role that you would have.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:51.540
Of course, in this role you would usually

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:54.740
crunch the numbers, conduct
interviews with clients,

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:56.120
create slide decks.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:57.290
So, this is really the role

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:59.090
where you learn the ropes of the trade.

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:01.120
And for this role in
a country like Germany

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:05.310
you can expect a salary of
roughly 70,000 Euro per year

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:07.820
for a master level
graduate, which is of course

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:10.660
a very decent starting
salary for a new graduate.

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:13.870
You will have this business
analyst role for about two years

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:16.940
and after two years most
of these TierOne Firms

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:18.610
offer something which is very unique

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:21.520
and this is the so-called leave program.

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:22.930
And here again how exactly it's called

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:24.550
differs a bit company by company

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:26.160
but what essentially it boils down to

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.470
is that the company will
give you the opportunity

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:29.960
to leave work again

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:33.370
and to spend some time to
conduct a PhD or an MBA

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:36.000
or often also social leave year

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.540
if you want to volunteer
for a social organization.

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:41.210
And this time, which usually
takes two to three years

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:43.810
we'll be heavily subsidized
by your employer.

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:45.350
So for instance, if you do an MBA

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:46.830
the company usually will sponsor

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:49.780
a significant portion of
the tuition of your MBA

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:51.800
and they will pay you money on top

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.850
often also up to a full salary

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:56.620
just to cover your living
expenses in this time.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:58.590
And here even within the TierOne Firms

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:00.450
there can be significant differences

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:04.220
in how exactly this program is
set up, how attractive it is.

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:06.270
What I learned now from
talking to other friends

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:09.030
probably the McKinsey one is
arguably the most attractive

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:12.140
then followed by the Boston
Consulting followed by the Bain.

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:13.630
And here also what I
want you to understand

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:15.880
is that many of these
smaller two-tier firms

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:18.200
offer programs like this as well.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:20.000
But then if you look into them off

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.670
they're not as attractive

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:23.630
or maybe they are saying,
yes, you can do that,

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:26.010
but then the end it turns out
that only if you're ranked

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:28.030
as one of the top top performers,

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:29.760
you will really be offered to do this.

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:31.910
And then the big majority
of consultants in the end

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:33.550
will not have this opportunity.

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:35.470
So, I'd argue that this
is really something

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:37.550
that on top of the
regular salary differences

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:40.470
really sets apart these tier-one firms

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:41.730
from these other firms

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:43.990
and you really should
take this into account

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:46.300
when you compare the
total compensation package

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:48.660
in the first years of
your time in consulting

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:50.950
because the value of
the compensation package

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:52.980
that you get in this leave program

00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:55.230
can easily be in the six digits.

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:57.410
So, really have a look at this closely

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:58.740
before you ask yourself

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:00.720
what company you wanna join after all.

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:01.740
Then after the leave

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:04.720
usually you enter an
associate type of position.

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:05.970
This is also the position

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:07.970
that you would directly be able to join

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:11.170
if you join consulting
with an MBA or with a PhD.

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:13.240
In terms of the contents of your job

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:14.980
this is pretty much just an extension

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:17.330
of what you were doing
as a business analyst

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:20.470
with the only difference that
now more is expected from you.

00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:21.960
So, you will be now expected

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:24.940
to lead larger parts of the project.

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:26.870
You will be expected now to do things

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:29.240
stand alone with very little guidance

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:32.940
from your project lead, just
the workload, the expectations,

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:36.510
the responsibilities you have
will just increase will expand

00:06:36.510 --> 00:06:37.750
compared to these other roles.

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:40.250
And as an associate,
you can expect to earn

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:43.770
around 110,000 Euro in Germany,

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:46.090
again with differences company by company.

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:48.880
So, this is indeed a
significant salary increase

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:50.060
to the role that you had earlier.

00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:51.580
Then this associate role is again

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:54.100
something that you will often
do for about two years or so

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:56.740
and then you advance and
the project lead role,

00:06:56.740 --> 00:06:58.980
this is now the role that
you will be responsible

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:02.460
for consulting teams working
on the ground and the client,

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:04.640
typically consulting
team is the project lead

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:06.610
plus one to four consultants.

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:08.860
So, total team of two to five consultants.

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:09.693
And then on top of course

00:07:09.693 --> 00:07:11.540
you'll also have the
Junior Partners, Partners,

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:12.880
Senior Partners who come on top

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:15.120
will provide some guidance
and join you occasionally.

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:17.980
So, as a project lead,
you can expect to 140

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:21.400
to 150,000 Euro base salary every year.

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:23.270
And then at the project lead level

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:26.040
with many firms also the
bonuses start to increase.

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:27.330
So, maybe you might have the potential

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:29.200
to earning approved 30%

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:32.040
or even more bonus on
top of your base salary

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:33.600
instead of maybe only 20

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:35.760
which was rather the norm
for the lower levels.

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:37.140
So, this is now the first level

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:38.370
where also the compensation

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:41.280
were very more significantly
based on your performance

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:43.017
that you will bring to
the table in your job.

00:07:43.017 --> 00:07:44.800
And after the project lead role

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:47.810
most firms distinguished
different levels of Partner roles.

00:07:47.810 --> 00:07:50.690
So, often it starts with
a Junior Partner level

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:52.680
which you will have for
another two years or so

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:55.720
until then you can get
elected Partner of the firm.

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:57.850
This is not as real full Partner role

00:07:57.850 --> 00:08:00.630
which is often the aspiration
of many, many people

00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:03.500
then still wanna continue
their career in consulting.

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.010
And then after four to five years

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:06.330
or so in your Partner role

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:07.990
you can become a Senior Partner,

00:08:07.990 --> 00:08:09.730
which is then in terms of job title

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:11.630
the highest level that you can reach.

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:13.290
So, when we discuss the salaries

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:14.670
of these different Partner levels,

00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:15.750
here it's important to understand

00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:18.310
that these salary structures
are getting much more complex.

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:20.050
So, besides a base salary

00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:22.220
off there is a component which is linked

00:08:22.220 --> 00:08:24.960
to the performance of the company overall.

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:27.520
So, how good is the company doing overall

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:28.690
that you're working for?

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:30.220
This will affect your salary

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:32.470
and then also your performance element.

00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:34.880
So, the bonus that you will
get paid on top of that

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:37.740
this will not pay an
increasingly important role

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:39.450
of your overall compensation.

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:41.490
But that being said as a Junior Partner,

00:08:41.490 --> 00:08:42.720
you can then expect to earn

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:46.120
something about 200 to 250,000 Euro

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:48.830
and then once you're really
getting elected to full Partner

00:08:48.830 --> 00:08:51.820
this will usually be above
300,000 Euro in salary.

00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:53.870
The salary will then increase over time

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:56.490
again, heavily also influenced
by your performance.

00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:57.830
Once you're a Senior Partner

00:08:57.830 --> 00:09:01.780
this can then be rather
around 600 to 800,000 Euro

00:09:01.780 --> 00:09:03.410
and indeed the best earning,

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:07.000
best performing Senior Partners
can earn in the millions.

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:09.740
So, will earn several
million Euro every year.

00:09:09.740 --> 00:09:12.020
Of course, while these
figures sound very high

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:13.320
it's also important to understand

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:16.060
that it's not necessarily
easy to become Partner.

00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:19.440
There's a so concept and idea
of the Up-or-Out Principle.

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:20.820
If you've never heard about that

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:23.860
I will link us a video above
here that I did on this topic.

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:26.450
So, in a nutshell, people
will get filtered out.

00:09:26.450 --> 00:09:28.600
Many people will get
asked to leave the firm

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:30.010
at some point in their career.

00:09:30.010 --> 00:09:32.030
Only the very best of course

00:09:32.030 --> 00:09:34.020
will have the opportunity
to become Partner

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:36.060
and then earn salaries
in these dimensions.

